 out of Sion; and may you see the prosperity of Jerusalem all the days of your life.","poem":1}]},{"type":"verse","number":6,"content":[{"lineBreak":true},{"text":"And may you see your children's children. Peace be upon Israel.","poem":1}]}],"footnotes":[{"noteId":232,"caller":"+","text":"Alex. fruits of your labours.","reference":{"chapter":127,"verse":2}}]},"thisChapterLink":"/api/eng_lxu/PSA/127.json","thisChapterAudioLinks":{},"nextChapterApiLink":"/api/eng_lxu/PSA/128.json","nextChapterAudioLinks":{},"previousChapterApiLink":"/api/eng_lxu/PSA/126.json","previousChapterAudioLinks":{},"numberOfVerses":6}